TI  - APPLICATION OF SEISMIC-ELECTRIC COUPLED TUNNEL ADVANCED GEOLOGICAL FORECASTING IN WATER-BEARING ROCK PROJECTS
T2  - FRESENIUS ENVIRONMENTAL BULLETIN
AB  - With the rapid development of China's transportation and water conservancy industry, a large number of tunnel projects appear. Geological disasters such as landslides and water gushing caused by adverse geological conditions often occur, causing serious damage to the surrounding ecosystem, causing great economic losses and security risks. As a joint prediction technology combining electrokinetic effect and TSP, TSEP has become a new method of ecological environment protection in underground tunnel engineering. This paper introduces the development status and basic principle of TSEP technology and discusses several key factors affecting TSEP data acquisition. The TSEP test was carried out in the lishanping tunnel of the Shuiqing section of Chongqing Kunming expressway, and the prediction results of TSEP were obtained. The results are consistent with the distribution of rock mass and water body in the subsequent excavation, which verifies the feasibility and effectiveness of the application of TSEP technology in the ecological environment protection of tunnel engineering.
