AU  - KESSLER, JJ
TI  - ATRIPLEX FORAGE AS A DRY SEASON SUPPLEMENTATION FEED FOR SHEEP IN THE MONTANE PLAINS OF THE YEMEN-ARAB-REPUBLIC
T2  - JOURNAL OF ARID ENVIRONMENTS
AB  - Sheep in the Yemen Arab Republic depend to a large extent on rangeland grazing. The effects were studied of the introduction of Atriplex nummularia forage as a dry season feed supplement. Sixteen percent of a sheep herd''s diet could consist of Atriplex forage if they fed on it for 30 min daily. Although the introduction of Atriplex forage did not lead to improved growth rates, its consumption prevented weight loss, as compared with the control herd which grazed unimproved pasture only. Re-vegetation of the Yemeni rangelands with Atriplex is recommended, considering also ecological advantages.
